hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1156","Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Al-Amash narrated to us, and Sallam bin Junada narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, said: A man came to Omar while he was at Arafat, and he said: O Commander of the Faithful! I came from Kufa, and I left there a man who dictated the Qur’an by heart. He said: Then Omar became angry and swollen until he almost filled the space between My two branches of travel, and he said: Who is he, Woe to you? He said: Abdullah bin Masoud. He said: And his anger continued to be released and extinguished until it returned to the state it was in. Then he said: Woe to you, what a shame! I know that there is no one more deserving of that than him, and I will tell you about that. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to stay with Abu Bakr. Tonight is the same with regard to the matter of the Muslims, and he stayed with him one night, and I was with him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out. He was walking, and we went out with him, and we saw a man standing and praying in the mosque, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and listened to his recitation. When we were about to We know the man. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is pleased to read the Qur’an properly as it was revealed, let him read it as Ibn Umm Abd,” he said: Then the man sat down to pray, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, started saying: “Ask and it will be given to him” twice, he said: Then Omar said: So I said: By God, I will go to him and give him good tidings. He said: So I went to him to give him good tidings, and I found that Abu Bakr had preceded me to him, so he gave him good tidings. No, by God. I never preceded him in doing good unless he preceded me. This is the hadith of Abu Musa, except that he did not say it and was puffed up, and Salam bin Junada said: He still continued to narrate it, and he said: He is standing in Arafat, and he did not He said: He continues, and he said: He listens to his recitation, and he said: Then Omar said: By God, I will return to him."
"1157","It was narrated to us by Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala, it was narrated to me by Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Bukair, it was narrated to me by al-Layth, H, it was narrated to me by Sa’id ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd. Al-Hakam, my father told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Yazid, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Makhramah bin Sulayman, that Kurayb A servant of Ibn Abbas told him, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas, and I said: What did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray at night? He said: “It was recited in some of his rooms, and whoever was outside could hear it.”"
